# Everything about how we work stays out of the public repo.
#
# One directory, one rule — deliberately a directory and not a file list.
# Listing documents by name fails quietly: a new report lands in the root,
# nobody remembers to add a line, and one `git add -A` publishes the internal
# analysis. A directory cannot be forgotten.
#
#   internal/reportes/   analysis and audit write-ups
#   internal/plan/       workplan, roadmaps
#   internal/pruebas/    manual test protocols
#   internal/archivo/    superseded versions
internal/

# Test artifacts
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Dev harness and the data it produces. Kept out of the package and out of the
# public repo: it hammers third-party portals and its outputs are large.
sweep/*.jsonl
sweep/*.log
sweep/out/
